if they occur as a natural result of discussion.
	I definately feel that people should refrain from advocating views that
oppose the list principles. However pointing out (putative) flaws in such things
as PPL or libertarianism is the very stuff of debate.
	I agree with you about the irritation of some recent postings. I may
be mildly collectivist, but I am certainly a hard-headed rationalist when it
comes to flying yogis and paganism and such. I do not know what should be done
with people who refuse to acknowledge polite requests, but I suggest that it
is a matter for the list administrator. I do not feel that removing people who
are not ExI members is a good idea. I am not an ExI member. For one thing, it
is a matter of some inconvenience to me, not having ready acess to US money.
But most importantly, there are important differences between the views of
myself, and the views of ExI. There are many similarities, enough to make me
read and post to this list. In an earlier flame war, after certain people (such
