Perhaps I could become an invited guest, but I don't favour this solution, as it
shuts out newcomers, and there is no clear way to gain membership other than
become an ExI member, which I have only heard of on this list.
	My final point. As to tolerance, there are no doubt many tolerant and
open-minded libertarians on this list, but there are certainly many intolerant
people, or at least people who shoot first and ask questions later (I'm also in
favour of gun-control for this very reason :-) (though not in America, only over
here, so no flames). In the flame war over socialism that I referred to, I made
the point several times that I was not saying that socialism was even a 
particularly good political philosophy (I am only a socialist when compared to
libertarians :-) but only that it was not OBVIOUSLY wrong. I received an 
large number of heated replies, bristling with examples of socialist evil, and
'proofs' of its falsehood. I simply fail to understand how educated intelligent
people can say that something believed after careful thought by millions of 
other educated intelligent people is OBVIOUSLY wrong. I still stand by my firm
belief that if socialism is a bad philosophy, the reasons for its wrongness are
either controversial and/or complicated. To assume that all those who believe
in something are idiots unable to see the obvious truth is the essence of 
